01:38:08.390 --> 01:38:09.700
That's cute. Say it again.

01:38:10.130 --> 01:38:13.090
He came here first to ask where Lola was. I made him come back. I was working on him.

01:38:13.860 --> 01:38:15.440
He's a crazy sort of guy, quick-tempered.

01:38:16.070 --> 01:38:18.090
I kept hammering into him that she was with another man

01:38:18.090 --> 01:38:21.230
so he'd go into one of his jealous ragers and then I'd tell him where she was.

01:38:22.590 --> 01:38:24.830
And you know what he would have done to her, don't you, Walter?

01:38:25.550 --> 01:38:28.640
Yeah. For once I believe you, because it's just rotten enough.

01:38:30.540 --> 01:38:31.240
We're both rotten.

01:38:32.350 --> 01:38:33.290
Only you're a little more rotten.

01:38:34.260 --> 01:38:35.640
You got me to take care of your husband for you.

01:38:36.200 --> 01:38:37.560
And then you get Zucchetti to take care of Alola.

01:38:37.760 --> 01:38:38.640
Maybe take care of me too.

01:38:39.770 --> 01:38:41.790
Then somebody else would have come along to take care of Zucchetti for you.

01:38:42.860 --> 01:38:44.020
That's the way you operate, isn't it, baby?

01:38:44.580 --> 01:38:45.280
Suppose it is.

01:38:45.550 --> 01:38:47.230
Is what you've got cooked up for tonight any better?

01:38:47.430 --> 01:38:50.840
I don't like that music anymore.

01:38:52.520 --> 01:38:53.220
Mind if I close the window?

01:39:14.330 --> 01:39:22.560
Can't you baby try it again if I came a little closer

01:39:34.440 --> 01:39:55.220
this think you can do it now shoot again baby don't tell me it's because you've been in love

01:39:55.220 --> 01:39:59.980
with me all this time no i never loved you walter not you were any

01:40:01.420 --> 01:40:03.940
I'm rotten to the heart I used you just as you said.

01:40:04.670 --> 01:40:05.970
That's all you ever meant to me.

01:40:06.070 --> 01:40:12.790
Until a minute ago, when I couldn't fire that second shot.

01:40:15.700 --> 01:40:17.160
I never thought that could happen to me.

01:40:19.280 --> 01:40:20.440
Sorry, baby, I'm not buying.

01:40:20.710 --> 01:40:21.950
I'm not asking you to buy.

01:40:21.990 --> 01:40:22.870
Just hold me close.

01:40:30.220 --> 01:40:30.780
Goodbye, baby.

01:41:30.030 --> 01:41:44.870
here i said come here name is nef yeah and i still don't like it what do you want

01:41:46.210 --> 01:41:49.230
Look, kid, I want to give you a present.

01:41:49.410 --> 01:41:51.370
Here's a nice new nickel.

01:41:52.120 --> 01:41:52.740
What's a gag?

01:41:53.150 --> 01:41:55.410
Suppose you go on back down the hill to the drugstore and make a phone call.

01:41:55.770 --> 01:41:57.590
Keep your nickel and buy yourself an ice cream cone.

01:41:57.810 --> 01:41:59.190
The number is granted 0386.

01:42:00.000 --> 01:42:01.800
That's for Miss Diedrichson. First name is Lola.

01:42:01.940 --> 01:42:03.310
She isn't worth a nickel.

01:42:03.470 --> 01:42:05.880
If I ever talk to her, she's not going to be over any telephone.

01:42:06.420 --> 01:42:06.880
Tough, aren't you?

01:42:07.290 --> 01:42:08.770
Here, take the nickel and call her. She wants you to.

01:42:08.950 --> 01:42:10.720
She doesn't want any part of it.

01:42:11.620 --> 01:42:13.170
I know who told you that. It's not true.

01:42:14.130 --> 01:42:14.770
Lola's in love with you.

01:42:15.000 --> 01:42:18.080
She always has been. Don't ask me why. I couldn't even guess.

01:42:18.860 --> 01:42:21.930
Here, granted 0386. I'll go on to call her.

01:42:22.070 --> 01:42:23.520
Go on, that way.

01:42:35.080 --> 01:42:36.460
Almost 4.30 now, Keyes.

01:42:41.670 --> 01:42:43.450
She's still lying alone up there in that house.

01:42:45.230 --> 01:42:46.270
They found her by now.

01:42:49.260 --> 01:42:51.860
A lot of things don't matter anymore.

01:42:56.750 --> 01:42:58.680
So I want you to do a favor for me, Keyes.

01:43:00.570 --> 01:43:01.810
I want you to be the one to tell Lola.

01:43:01.950 --> 01:43:04.580
Kind of gently, before it breaks wide open.

01:43:04.780 --> 01:43:09.420
I want you to take care of her and that guy, Sekedi.

01:43:15.540 --> 01:43:17.150
He doesn't get pushed around too much.

01:43:20.300 --> 01:43:20.540
For keys.

01:43:31.660 --> 01:43:33.660
I'll put it early on ya.

01:43:35.308 --> 01:43:36.648
Wonder what time you got down at the office.

01:43:39.404 --> 01:43:41.404
That little man of yours pulled you out of bed

01:43:42.316 --> 01:43:43.156
the janitor did.

01:43:44.876 --> 01:43:47.076
Seems you leaked a little blood on the way in here.

01:43:49.292 --> 01:43:50.292
You won't be surprised.

01:43:53.292 --> 01:43:56.292
I wanted to straighten the other in that Diederson case.

01:43:56.332 --> 01:43:57.092
So I get it.

01:43:59.500 --> 01:44:00.000
long you've been standing.

01:44:00.000 --> 01:44:07.860
that long enough kind of a crazy story with a crazy twist to it when you didn't quite figure out

01:44:07.860 --> 01:44:17.710
well you can't figure them all walter but i guess you can't have that because i get the big speech

01:44:17.710 --> 01:44:29.980
with all the two dollar words in it let's have it case walter washed up

01:44:32.680 --> 01:44:34.220
Thanks, Keyes. I was short anyway.

01:44:36.640 --> 01:44:37.700
I'm going to call for a doctor.

01:44:40.960 --> 01:44:43.390
For? So they can patch me up?

01:44:44.500 --> 01:44:46.180
So they can nurse me along till I get back on my feet?

01:44:46.360 --> 01:44:49.710
So I can walk into that gas chamber up at San Quentin on my own power?

01:44:50.720 --> 01:44:51.380
Is that it, Keyes?

01:44:52.340 --> 01:44:53.220
Something like that.

01:44:53.340 --> 01:44:55.800
A different idea.

01:44:56.660 --> 01:44:56.820
Yeah?

01:44:57.450 --> 01:44:59.980
Look, Keyes, suppose you went back to...

01:45:00.000 --> 01:45:02.920
Didn't find these cylinders till tomorrow morning when the office opens.

01:45:04.040 --> 01:45:05.320
After that, you can play it any way you like.

01:45:06.700 --> 01:45:07.760
Would you do that much for me, Keyes?

01:45:07.980 --> 01:45:10.700
Give me one good reason.

01:45:11.560 --> 01:45:12.900
I need four hours to get where I'm going.

01:45:13.550 --> 01:45:14.730
You're not going anywhere, Walter.

01:45:15.990 --> 01:45:18.490
I bet I am. Across the border.

01:45:18.740 --> 01:45:20.180
You haven't got a chance, Walter.

01:45:20.630 --> 01:45:21.770
Good luck to try for it.

01:45:22.240 --> 01:45:23.340
You'll never make the border.

01:45:24.300 --> 01:45:24.960
That's what you think.

01:45:26.550 --> 01:45:27.030
Watch me.

01:45:28.410 --> 01:45:29.710
You'll never even make the elevator.

01:45:30.990 --> 01:45:31.510
So long, Keys.

01:46:01.500 --> 01:46:05.450
Hello, send an ambulance to the Pacific Building on Olive Street.

01:46:07.390 --> 01:46:09.430
Yeah, it's a police job.

01:46:09.930 --> 01:46:29.970
What are you doing here?

01:46:34.580 --> 01:46:36.500
Somebody moved the elevator a couple of miles away.

01:46:38.340 --> 01:46:39.020
You're on the way.

01:46:44.530 --> 01:46:45.750
You know why you couldn't figure this one, Keyes?

01:46:47.010 --> 01:46:47.530
I'll tell you.

01:46:49.060 --> 01:46:50.860
Because the guy you were looking for was too close.

01:46:51.080 --> 01:46:53.780
He had to cross the desk from you.

01:46:55.360 --> 01:46:56.480
Closer than that, Walter.

01:47:01.470 --> 01:47:01.990
I love you too.
